// Cloud Model Comparison (exam reference)
// IaaS → EC2, VPC, EBS — you manage OS and above
// PaaS → Elastic Beanstalk, RDS, Lambda — AWS manages runtime
// SaaS → Amazon WorkMail, Chime — AWS manages everything

// CapEx vs OpEx:
// CapEx: Buy servers upfront → large initial investment, depreciate over time
// OpEx: Pay monthly AWS bill → predictable, tied to usage, no idle capacity

// Deployment models:
// Public Cloud  → fully on AWS (most common)
// Private Cloud → on-premises (e.g., VMware)
// Hybrid Cloud  → mix of on-prem + AWS (common during migration)

// AWS Global Infrastructure Hierarchy:
//
// GLOBAL SERVICES (not Region-specific):
//   IAM, Route 53, CloudFront, WAF (global), Shield
//
// REGIONAL SERVICES (replicate across AZs within Region):
//   S3 (data stored in region, accessed globally)
//   DynamoDB, Lambda, SQS, SNS, API Gateway
//   ECS, EKS (control plane)
//
// AZ-SPECIFIC SERVICES:
//   EC2 instances, EBS volumes
//   RDS instances (but Multi-AZ spans 2 AZs)
//   ElastiCache nodes
//   Subnet (each subnet lives in exactly one AZ)
//
// EDGE LOCATIONS (400+):
//   CloudFront distributions (CDN)
//   Route 53 (anycast DNS)
//   AWS Shield, WAF (at edge)

// SHARED RESPONSIBILITY MODEL — Quick Reference Table
//
// ┌─────────────────────┬─────────────────┬─────────────────┐
// │ Responsibility      │ EC2 (IaaS)      │ RDS (Managed)   │
// ├─────────────────────┼─────────────────┼─────────────────┤
// │ Physical hardware   │ AWS             │ AWS             │
// │ Hypervisor/host OS  │ AWS             │ AWS             │
// │ Guest OS patching   │ CUSTOMER        │ AWS             │
// │ DB engine patching  │ CUSTOMER        │ AWS             │
// │ Network controls    │ CUSTOMER        │ CUSTOMER        │
// │ IAM / access mgmt   │ CUSTOMER        │ CUSTOMER        │
// │ Data encryption     │ CUSTOMER        │ CUSTOMER        │
// │ Application code    │ CUSTOMER        │ CUSTOMER        │
// │ Security groups     │ CUSTOMER        │ CUSTOMER        │
// └─────────────────────┴─────────────────┴─────────────────┘
//
// MEMORY AID:
// AWS = Security OF the cloud (hardware, facilities, global network)
// You  = Security IN the cloud (your data, your configs, your IAM)
//
// Lambda shared responsibility:
// AWS: Runtime env, underlying OS, hardware, auto-scaling infrastructure
// You: Function code, IAM execution role, env variable secrets, VPC config

// IAM Policy JSON — S3 read-only with MFA condition
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Sid": "AllowS3ReadWithMFA",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "s3:GetObject",
        "s3:GetObjectVersion",
        "s3:ListBucket",
        "s3:GetBucketLocation"
      ],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:s3:::my-secure-bucket",
        "arn:aws:s3:::my-secure-bucket/*"
      ],
      "Condition": {
        "Bool": {
          "aws:MultiFactorAuthPresent": "true"
        },
        "NumericLessThan": {
          "aws:MultiFactorAuthAge": "3600"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "Sid": "DenyAllWithoutMFA",
      "Effect": "Deny",
      "Action": "s3:*",
      "Resource": "*",
      "Condition": {
        "BoolIfExists": {
          "aws:MultiFactorAuthPresent": "false"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}

