// Aurora vs RDS Multi-AZ — Key Differences:
//
// Aurora:
//   Storage: Distributed across 3 AZs automatically
//   Replicas: Up to 15 (low lag, auto-promote on failure)
//   Failover: ~30 seconds (no data transfer needed)
//   Scaling: Storage auto-scales; Serverless v2 for compute
//   Cost: ~20% more than standard RDS for same instance class
//
// RDS Multi-AZ:
//   Storage: Synchronous standby in different AZ
//   Replicas: Up to 5 read replicas separately
//   Failover: ~60-120 seconds
//   Scaling: Manual storage scaling; reserved instances
//   Cost: Lower base cost than Aurora

