// EXAM DECISION GUIDE — SQS vs SNS vs EventBridge vs Kinesis
//
// Scenario → Recommended Service:
//
// "Decouple app components, handle traffic spikes"
// → SQS (queue buffer, pull-based)
//
// "One event, notify 5 different services simultaneously"
// → SNS + SQS fan-out (publish once, fan to queues)
//
// "AWS service events (EC2 state change, S3 upload) trigger Lambda"
// → EventBridge (CloudWatch Events)
//
// "Process 100,000 IoT sensor readings per second, maintain order"
// → Kinesis Data Streams (sharded stream, high throughput)
//
// "Email/SMS notifications to users"
// → SNS (email, SMS subscriptions)
//
// "Order must be processed exactly once, in order"
// → SQS FIFO (exactly-once, ordered, MessageGroupId)
//
// "Replay last hour of events for debugging"
// → Kinesis (24hr-7day retention, replay supported)
//
// "Microservices emit business events, other services subscribe"
// → EventBridge custom event bus
//
