// EXAM QUICK-REFERENCE CHEAT SHEET
//
// HIGH AVAILABILITY vs READ SCALING:
// Multi-AZ RDS   → HA (failover), standby not readable
// Read Replicas  → Read scaling, not for failover
// Aurora Global  → Cross-region HA + read scaling
//
// ENCRYPTION:
// S3: SSE-S3 (free), SSE-KMS (audit), SSE-C (bring key)
// EBS: KMS, must enable at creation
// RDS: KMS, must enable at creation (can't enable later)
// DynamoDB: KMS (default encryption with AWS-owned key)
// Lambda env vars: encrypted by KMS
//
// COLD START SOLUTIONS FOR JAVA LAMBDA:
// SnapStart (Java 21) + Provisioned Concurrency
//
// COMMON GOTCHAS:
// Q: Need to block a specific IP → NACL (not Security Group)
// Q: EC2 needs S3 access without credentials → IAM Instance Profile
// Q: Lambda can't reach DynamoDB in VPC → VPC Endpoint (Gateway)
// Q: SQS message reappears after processing → Visibility timeout too short
//    OR forgot to call DeleteMessage
// Q: S3 eventual consistency → It's NOW strongly consistent (since 2020)
// Q: Lambda async retries → 2 retries (3 total attempts) then DLQ
